; The development preview surface's declared entry names, and the tokens that
; must never reach a gameplay product.
;
; Source: HarkenEngine/Source/Tooling/Preview/include/harken_preview/PreviewAbi.h
; Check:  py -3 HarkenEngine/Source/Tooling/Preview/abi/check_preview_isolation.py
;
; Why a manifest for a static library. Nothing links this file: harken_preview is
; a static library, so no linker needs an export list. What needs one is the
; review. The gameplay export allowlist (HarkenEngine/Source/Runtime/api/abi/
; HarkenCore.def) and the C# binding under HarkenIntegration/Unity/Harken/Runtime/Generated/ are both
; emitted from the engine's own public declarations, and those generators never
; read the preview header -- so the isolation holds structurally, with no filter
; to configure and none to forget. That is a good property and a silent one: it
; is invisible in a diff, and it would be lost the moment a preview entry were
; declared in the public header instead, with every existing check still green.
;
; This file makes it stateable from the preview side. EXPORTS is the surface's
; own entry set, kept in step with the header in both directions: an entry the
; header declares and this file omits fails the check, and so does the reverse.
; ISOLATED-TOKENS is what the check then looks for in the gameplay products and
; in the two inputs they are generated from, so a preview name appearing in the
; public header or the wire table is a red check at the moment it appears --
; before anyone regenerates anything.

EXPORTS
    VnPreview_CancelProject
    VnPreview_CapturePlaybackPaths
    VnPreview_CommitProject
    VnPreview_DrainProjectAcks
    VnPreview_EnableChannelPeakMetering
    VnPreview_HasAction
    VnPreview_HasPlayableConsumers
    VnPreview_PlayPlayable
    VnPreview_PlayVoiceRaw
    VnPreview_PrepareProject
    VnPreview_PrepareProjectV2
    VnPreview_PrepareProjectV3
    VnPreview_ProjectIsOpen
    VnPreview_PumpNullMixer
    VnPreview_QueryOwnerRevision
    VnPreview_QueryPlayable
    VnPreview_RefreshVoiceBindings
    VnPreview_RegisterPcm
    VnPreview_ResetPlayable
    VnPreview_SetVoiceProperty
    VnPreview_StopPlayable
    VnPreview_TakeChannelPeaks

; The identifier prefixes and the capability name this surface owns. A token
; here appearing anywhere in a gameplay product, or in a generator input, means
; the surface has crossed into the production face.
ISOLATED-TOKENS
    VnPreview
    VN_PREVIEW_
    HARKEN_PREVIEW_CAPABILITY
    development-preview
